    "quote": "Manufacturers must report every thermal incident involving overheating, fire, injury, or material property damage to the responsible regulator within 24 hours of learning of it, with a preliminary account of known circumstances and affected units. Manufacturers must notify affected customers within 48 hours when an incident indicates a potential safety risk to their model or installed units, and promptly provide updates and recommended protective steps."
   },
