    "results_to_customers": "numeric_rates",
    "public_publication": false,
    "quote": "Each model must undergo a sustained-heat test at 55 °C using a regulator-approved protocol. The maximum permitted failure rate is 7% per model. A model exceeding 5% must submit a corrective-action plan to the regulator and complete retesting within 12 months; regulators may require interim protective measures based on risk. A model exceeding 7% may not be newly marketed until corrective action and retesting demonstrate compliance."
   },
